<page type="text"><layout>One page of text in two columns: left column of verse running from top to the bottom edge of the scan; right column of verse at top, short, cut off. Running head at top centre; page number top right. Marginal specks only, no notes.; One column of italic verse in the centre of the page, with a catchword line "In" at the foot right; in the left margin a short note block at the bottom left ("Tom. II." and a running line in the margin).</layout><page_number>681 / rrrr</page_number><running_head>BABYLONIS MAGNÆ.</running_head><bottom_margin><catchword>In</catchword></bottom_margin><main_text><l>De Presbyterorum numero</l>
    <l>Damnabili revera.</l>
    <l>Omnes ad Clericalia</l>
    <l>Recurrunt, ut per talia,</l>
    <l>Quæ sua sunt, acquirant:</l>
    <l><i>Messiam non inveniunt,</i></l>
    <l><i>Nec invenire cupiunt</i></l>
    <l><i>Spontaneè delirant.</i></l>
    <l>De Christi patrimonio,</l>
    <l><i>Sub pompis &amp; præconio</i></l>
    <l><i>Viventes, intumescunt:</i></l>
    <l><i>Intenti voluptatibus,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et mundi vanitatibus,</i></l>
    <l><i>De cappis erubescunt.</i></l>
    <l><i>Non solum noto Monachos,</i></l>
    <l><i>Sed etiam Canonicos,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et fictas Moniales:</i></l>
    <l><i>Quæ propter Jesu minimè,</i></l>
    <l><i>Videntur esse filiæ,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et filii spirituales:</i></l>
    <l><i>Sed magis, ut divitiis</i></l>
    <l><i>Fruantur, &amp; deliciis,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et cæteris cupitis.</i></l>
    <l><i>Quæ replicare nequeo,</i></l>
    <l><i>Nec volo, neque debeo</i></l>
    <l><i>De istis hypocritis.</i></l>
    <l><i>A quibus multa patitur</i></l>
    <l><i>Confunditur, &amp; quatitur</i></l>
    <l><i>Navicula marina,</i></l>
    <l><i>In qua dormit jã Dominus,</i></l>
    <l><i>Quem suscitat discipulus</i></l>
    <l><i>Et postulat divina.</i></l>
    <l>Es Clericis &amp; laicis,</l>
    <l>In mundo constituti:</l>
    <l>Impellitur manicula</l>
  <p cont="true"><i>Iam tanta sunt pericula,</i><br /></p>
    <p><i>Quòd vix spes est salutis.</i></p>
    <p><i>Vix tamen surgit aliquis,</i><br /><i>Et rogat Dominum pro iis</i><br /><i>Periculis, instanter:</i><br /><i>Ne navis Sanctæ fidei</i><br /><i>Mergatur ab hypocrisi,</i><br /><i>Quæ regnat abundanter.</i></p>
    <p><i>In cunctis terræ finibus,</i><br /><i>In ventis &amp; turbinibus</i><br /><i>Innumeris, tam dirè:</i><br /><i>Quod nisi Deus faciat</i><br /><i>De speciali gratia,</i><br /><i>Timendum est perire.</i></p>
    <p><i>In die propinquissimo</i><br /><i>Zizania cum tritico,</i><br /><i>Et è controverso quidem:</i><br /><i>Nam Satan est in foribus,</i><br /><i>Et in mille coloribus,</i><br /><i>Ad destruendam fidem,</i><br /><i>Quam Christus suo sanguine</i><br /><i>Construxit in examine</i><br /><i>Cruentæ passionis:</i><br /><i>Dum perfidos damnaverat,</i><br /><i>Et credulos salvaverat</i><br /><i>In propriis personis.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quid amplius edisferam,</i><br /><i>Si vera loqui debeam;</i><br /><i>De vita Clericorum:</i><br /><i>Prælati sedent hodie</i></p>
    <p><i>Ve mundo nunc à scandalis,</i><br /><i>Tom. II.</i></p>
  </main_text><notes>Right column text is cut off at the scan edge; last line of the right column is partly illegible. Lines of the left column in verse set in italic and roman as printed. The running head is in capitals; the page number 681 is printed with a damaged final digit. Upper part of the page is cut off; the first line is a fragment. The left-margin marginal text at the bottom left is partly damaged and only partly legible. Verse lines are italic with long s written as s.</notes></page>
